---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site, standards, promises } from '../data/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy: How We Write | CheckVitalsNow"
  description="How CheckVitalsNow researches, writes, fact-checks, and updates its health and wellness guides, and the rules every guide follows."
  h1="Editorial Policy: How We Research and Write"
>
  <p>
    Health information should be easy to read and easy to check. This page explains how our guides are made, so you can
    decide how much to trust them.
  </p>

  <h2>Our standards</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      standards.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{s.name}:</strong> {s.text}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Where our information comes from</h2>
  <p>We start with sources that are accountable for what they publish:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      U.S. government health agencies, such as the National Institutes of Health (including NIDDK, NIMH, and the Office of
      Dietary Supplements), the CDC, the Office on Women's Health, and MedlinePlus.
    </li>
    <li>Academic medical centers and clinics, such as Mayo Clinic and Cleveland Clinic.</li>
    <li>Peer-reviewed studies and reviews, usually found through PubMed and PubMed Central.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every guide ends with a list of the sources it relies on, linked so you can read them yourself. We do not cite a
    study unless we have confirmed that it exists and says what we report.
  </p>

  <h2>How a guide is written</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>We start from the real question a reader is asking and answer it near the top of the page.</li>
    <li>We research the topic in the sources above and note where they agree, disagree, or have little evidence.</li>
    <li>We write in plain language, explain medical terms, and include practical steps where they are supported.</li>
    <li>We add a section on warning signs and when to see a doctor.</li>
    <li>Before publishing, we check every number, recommendation, and source link against the original.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Rules every guide follows</h2>
  <ul>
    {promises.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is independent. No company pays for or reviews our guides before they are published, and our guides do
    not link to products for sale. If we ever show advertising, ads will be clearly separated from our content and will
    have no influence on what we write.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Medical guidance changes. Each guide shows when it was published and when it was last updated, and we review guides
    when major sources change their advice. If you find an error, please tell us through our
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We will check it and, if we got something wrong, correct it.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
